<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karađorđević dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1804">1804</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Karađorđević dynasty was a Serbian royal house founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karadorde">Karađorđe Petrović</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-serbian-uprising">First Serbian Uprising</a> of 1804. It alternated in power with the rival Obrenović family in the 19th century, regained the Serbian throne under Peter I after the May Coup of 1903, and ruled the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> from 1918 until the monarchy was abolished in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karadordevic-dynasty.jpg" alt="Karađorđević dynasty" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Љубодраг Грујић · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Pavilion_Arms_of_the_Royal_Family_of_Karadjordjevic_of_Serbia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
